  "text": "\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n August 4, 2026 Lone Tree Community School District Special Election | Johnson County\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n \n \n \n Skip to main content\n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n \n\n Meetings and Agendas\n \n \n\n County News\n \n \n\n Event Calendar\n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n \n\n \n \n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n \n\n I Need To\n \n \n\n Apply for a grant or submit a bid\n \n \n\n Find County contact information\n \n \n\n Fill out a form\n \n \n\n Find a job\n \n \n\n Get a free gun lock\n \n \n\n Get a permit\n \n \n\n Pay court fines\n \n \n\n Pay taxes or fees\n \n \n\n Register a vehicle\n \n \n\n Renew my driver's license\n \n \n\n Request public records\n \n \n\n Serve jury duty\n \n \n \n \n \n\n County Groups\n \n \n\n Department Directory & Resources\n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n \n \n\n \n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n \n\n \n\n\n\n\nSearch\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n \n \n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\nAugust 4, 2026 Lone Tree Community School District Special Election\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n \n \n \n\n \n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n \n \n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n \n \n\n Home\n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n \n \n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n \n \n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\nResults\nVida Wollrab 302\nAlex Lorack 299\nJamie Lorack 152\nWrite In\n\nTotal voters: 419\nRegistration: 1437\nTurnout: 29%\nPrecinct Results\nTwo school board director seats to fill vacancies. The top vote getter will serve a term ending in November 2029. The second place candidate will serve a term ending in November 2027. In the event of a tie, lots are drawn by the Board of Supervisors at the canvass.\nFriday, July 10: Filing deadline. 17 signatures required. State law has recently changed and candidates will file with the Auditor's Office, not with the school district. \nCandidates - Updated through filing deadline 5 p.m. July 10\n\nSample Ballot\nAlex Lorack\n5952 Utah Ave SE\nLone Tree IA 52755\n319-331-6198\n[email protected] \nJamie Lorack\n5545 680th St SE\nNichols IA 52766\n319-330-3061\n[email protected] \nVida Wollrab\n211 S Perkins St\nLone Tree IA 52755\n319-629-5120\n319-471-3720\n[email protected] \nMonday, July 20: First day for early voting at Auditor's Office. Early voting will be available weekdays 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. \nMonday, July 20: Deadline to request mailed ballots. Forms must be in our office by 5 p.m. In person early voting will still be available after this date. \nMonday, July 20: Voter pre-registration deadline, 5 p.m. Voter registration is still available after this date using the election day registration procedure. \nMonday, August 3: Last day for in person early voting at the Auditor's Office. \nTuesday, August 4: Election Day. All voters will vote at the Lone Tree American Legion. Polls open 7 a.m. to 8 p.m.\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n \n \n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\nNeed to talk to someone from the county?\n\n\nContact Us \n\n \n\n\n\n \n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n \n\n Title VI and ADA Resources\n \n \n\n About Johnson County\n \n \n\n Contact\n \n \n\n Email subscriptions\n \n \n\n American Rescue Plan Act\n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n \n \n \n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n \n